<folder_context path="internal">

<reusable_module_context name="schema 2 lifecycle">
The lifecycle package owns init, add, pull, remove, and list. Manifest and lock readers accept
only schema 2. Cache and fetch are private implementation details, never additional commands.
</reusable_module_context>

<system_invariant name="recoverable dependency transactions">
Add and each pull process one dependency transaction containing all saved concrete bindings and
the optional surface. Preflight every binding before mutation. Snapshot owned native files and
Git metadata, restore them on adapter, metadata, or cache failure, and write the lock only after
all bindings succeed. Pull-all uses a common read-only preflight and stable alias order; earlier
successful dependency transactions may remain committed if a later dependency fails.
Adapter inspection classifies manager-owned lock or materialization drift as repairable so Pull
can converge a fresh, missing, or stale environment. Non-repairable declaration drift remains a
preflight error and is never overwritten.
</system_invariant>

<system_invariant name="prospective state before adapters">
Before invoking a mutating adapter operation, validate the complete prospective declaration and
lock, their cross-references, the existing lock, concrete capabilities, required tools, and local
conflicts. Preparation uses a copy of the loaded manifest; a failed dependency must not leak
bindings into a later pull-all write.
</system_invariant>

<system_invariant name="saved adapter identity">
Bindings are identified by adapter, concrete variant, and export. More than one implementation
may consume the same export ecosystem, such as Maven and Gradle consuming a maven export. Resolve
the implementation from the saved concrete variant; never let registry order or changed marker
files silently choose a different implementation.
Initial selection passes the requested dependency Git source and module path into Capability;
source-shape validation must not run against an incomplete placeholder dependency.
</system_invariant>

<system_invariant name="exact Git object bytes">
Fetch manifests, Agent Cards, and surfaces from the one resolved Git commit. Hash manifest bytes
from the Git object, not a translated worktree. Surface extraction excludes Git metadata,
untracked content, traversal, and symlinks and materializes below .git-a2a/surfaces/ALIAS.
Repository-relative Agent Cards are read relative to the upstream manifest root at that commit,
stored byte-identically as recoverable local metadata, and represented in lock/list by both the
declared reference and a usable consumer-local resolved path with Git provenance. HTTPS cards
remain external references and are not fetched.
</system_invariant>

<verification_and_unit_test_criteria>
Cover fresh clone without lock/cache, branch advance, unchanged pull, pull-one isolation,
polyglot rollback, saved variant mismatch, dirty submodule refusal, root and nested surfaces,
offline list, and full adapter Remove. Schema 1 and every removed command fail before mutation.
</verification_and_unit_test_criteria>

</folder_context>
